  (reduced from fuzz seed 2029):

    C4 = {a0, a1}, r1(a0, a1), not-C2(a1),
    T2 = not-C4 and (at most 1 inverse r0.C2),
    T5 = not-C0 and (some inverse r2.C1) and (all r1.C2) and (at most 1 r1.C1)

  T5 is not below T2: a1 can be an instance of T5 (it has no r1-successors) and a1 is in C4.
  In the test of T5 and not-T2, the choice C4 = {a0, a1} merged a0 into the test node; the role
  assertion r1(a0, a1) was then expanded from the backend cache with the deterministic base
  dependency instead of the dependency of the merge, so the clash of (all r1.C2) with not-C2(a1)
